%S A123455 1,2,4,11,33,147,896,8682,131293,3059990,104845237,5070719310,
%T A123455 334705459540
%N A123455 Number of slightly triangulated perfect graphs on n nodes.
%C A123455 A graph is slightly triangulated if it contains no hole of length at least 5 and every induced subgraph has a vertex whose neighborhood contains no induced path on 4 vertices. All such graphs are perfect (Hougardy, 2006). - _Meghanto Majumder_, Sep 30 2026
%H A123455 S. Hougardy, <a href="http://www.or.uni-bonn.de/~hougardy/">Home Page</a>
